 using it removes the specialization.","-Ensure it fixes the specialization and does not introduce a data-dependent error","-that converts to a graph break at or before the specialization location","-you are trying to  avoid. It might be better to use the next option.","+The {func}`torch._dynamo.decorators.mark_unbacked` function marks a tensor dimension","+as unbacked, so its concrete value is not used for specialization. Operations on","+that dimension must support unbacked symbols. For conditions that cannot be","+resolved at compile time, use explicit handling such as `guard_or_false`,","+`guard_or_true`, or `statically_known_true` when their semantics are appropriate.","+Otherwise, attempting to guard on the dimension can cause a data-dependent error","+or a graph break. See","+{ref}`troubleshooting_guardondatadependentsymnode_errors` for guidance on diagnosing","+and resolving these errors."," "," (dynamic_sources_allow_list)="," #### Dynamic Allow List (`DYNAMIC_SOURCES`)"],"additions":9,"deletions":6,"truncated":false},{"path":"test/distributed/tensor/test_compile_on_one_rank.py","lines":["@@ -2235,11 +2235,8 @@ def f(x):"," ","     @unittest.skipIf(not torch.accelerator.is_available(), \"requires accelerator\")","     @compiler_config.patch(compile_on_one_rank=True)","-    def test_device_index_symbol_is_not_size_like(self):","-        # The index is unbacked, but it is not a *size*. Allocating it with","-        # new_dynamic_size() files it under ShapeEnv.size_like, which carries the","-        # size-oblivious assumption that a value is never 0 or 1 -- here, that this","-        # rank is never cuda:0 or cuda:1.","+    def test_device_index_symbol_preserves_zero_one(self):","+        # Accelerator indices zero and one must remain valid symbolic values.","         from torch._subclasses.fake_tensor import FakeTensorMode","         from torch.fx.experimental.symbolic_shapes import ShapeEnv"," ","@@ -2247,9 +2244,10 @@ def test_device_index_symbol_is_not_si